### SignLik Backend API Testing
### You can run these requests directly in IntelliJ IDEA
### Base URL: http://localhost:8081

### ============================================
### AUTHENTICATION ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 1. Register a new user (DEAF)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john_doe",
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "DEAF"
}

### 2. Register another user (HEARING)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "jane_smith",
  "email": "jane@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "role": "HEARING"
}

### 3. Login with registered user (returns JWT token)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. Login with wrong password (should fail)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "john@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### ============================================
### USER ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 5. Get user profile by email
GET http://localhost:8081/api/users/profile/john@example.com

### 6. Update user profile
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/users/profile/john@example.com
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john_updated",
  "password": "newpassword123"
}

### 7. Search users by query
GET http://localhost:8081/api/users/search?query=john

### 8. Get all users
GET http://localhost:8081/api/users/all

### ============================================
### MESSAGE ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 9. Send a TEXT message
POST http://localhost:8081/api/messages/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Hello, how are you?",
  "type": "TEXT",
  "sender": {
    "username": "john_doe",
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "DEAF"
  },
  "receiver": {
    "username": "jane_smith",
    "email": "jane@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "HEARING"
  }
}

### 10. Send a SIGN message
POST http://localhost:8081/api/messages/send
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "👋🤟 (Hello in sign language)",
  "type": "SIGN",
  "sender": {
    "username": "john_doe",
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "DEAF"
  },
  "receiver": {
    "username": "jane_smith",
    "email": "jane@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "HEARING"
  }
}

### 11. Get all messages
GET http://localhost:8081/api/messages/all

### 12. Get messages by user email
GET http://localhost:8081/api/messages/user/john@example.com

### 13. Get conversation between two users
GET http://localhost:8081/api/messages/conversation?user1=john@example.com&user2=jane@example.com

### 14. Get messages by type (TEXT, VOICE, or SIGN)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/messages/type/TEXT

### 15. Get message by index
GET http://localhost:8081/api/messages/0

### 16. Delete message by index
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/messages/0

### 16.1. Forward a message to another user
POST http://localhost:8081/api/messages/forward?originalMessageId=1&fromEmail=john@example.com&toEmail=jane@example.com
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 17. Get paginated messages (with JWT token)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/messages/paginated?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
### TESTING WITH JWT TOKEN
### ============================================
### Note: After login, copy the token from the response and use it in the Authorization header
### Format: Authorization: Bearer <your-token-here>
###
### Example:
### 1. First login to get token
### 2. Copy the token from login response
### 3. Use it in protected endpoints like:
###    GET http://localhost:8081/api/messages/all
###    Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiJ9...

### ============================================
### FILE UPLOAD/DOWNLOAD ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 18. Upload a file (requires JWT token)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/files/upload
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="test.mp3"
Content-Type: audio/mpeg

< ./test.mp3
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="folder"

voice
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--

### 19. Get signed URL for file (expiring link)
GET http://localhost:8081/api/files/url/voice/abc123_test.mp3
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 20. Download file
GET http://localhost:8081/api/files/download/voice/abc123_test.mp3
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 21. Delete file
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/files/voice/abc123_test.mp3
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
### MESSAGES WITH ATTACHMENTS & CONVERSION
### ============================================

### 22. Send VOICE message with attachment (triggers STT conversion)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/messages/send
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Voice message",
  "type": "VOICE",
  "attachmentUrl": "voice/abc123_audio.mp3",
  "sender": {
    "username": "john_doe",
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "DEAF"
  },
  "receiver": {
    "username": "jane_smith",
    "email": "jane@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "HEARING"
  }
}

### 23. Send SIGN message with video attachment (triggers Sign-to-Text conversion)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/messages/send
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "Sign language message",
  "type": "SIGN",
  "attachmentUrl": "sign/xyz789_video.mp4",
  "sender": {
    "username": "john_doe",
    "email": "john@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "DEAF"
  },
  "receiver": {
    "username": "jane_smith",
    "email": "jane@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "role": "HEARING"
  }
}


### ============================================
### NOTIFICATION ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 24. Get all notifications
GET http://localhost:8081/api/notifications
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 25. Get unread notifications
GET http://localhost:8081/api/notifications/unread
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 26. Get unread notification count
GET http://localhost:8081/api/notifications/unread-count
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 27. Mark notification as read
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/notifications/1/read
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 28. Mark all notifications as read
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 29. Delete notification
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/notifications/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
### FRIENDSHIP ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 30. Send friend request
POST http://localhost:8081/api/friends/request?toEmail=jane@example.com
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 31. Accept friend request
PUT http://localhost:8081/api/friends/accept/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 32. Reject friend request
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/friends/reject/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 33. Remove friend
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/friends/remove?friendEmail=jane@example.com
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 34. Get all friends
GET http://localhost:8081/api/friends
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 35. Get pending friend requests
GET http://localhost:8081/api/friends/pending
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
### MESSAGE REACTIONS ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 36. Add reaction to message
POST http://localhost:8081/api/reactions/message/1?reaction=👍
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 37. Remove reaction from message
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/reactions/message/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 38. Get all reactions for a message
GET http://localhost:8081/api/reactions/message/1
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
### GROUP CONVERSATION ENDPOINTS
### ============================================

### 39. Create a group
POST http://localhost:8081/api/groups/create?name=Deaf Community&description=Group for deaf users
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 40. Add member to group
POST http://localhost:8081/api/groups/1/members?userEmail=jane@example.com&role=MEMBER
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 41. Remove member from group
DELETE http://localhost:8081/api/groups/1/members?userEmail=jane@example.com
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 42. Get my groups
GET http://localhost:8081/api/groups/my-groups
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### 43. Get group members
GET http://localhost:8081/api/groups/1/members
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

### ============================================
### MESSAGE SEARCH
### ============================================

### 44. Search messages
GET http://localhost:8081/api/messages/search?query=hello&userEmail=john@example.com
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE
